## Summary
Added two read-only, caller-permission-scoped P9.2 chat AI tools to `a2e-chat`:

- **`summarize-channel`** — reads a channel (or one thread via `threadParentId`) through the caller-context Core API client, returns chronological messages (`id`, author name, `createdAt`, `body`) plus participant and emoji-reaction stats.
- **`catch-me-up`** — returns the caller's unread backlog; window defaults to `chatReadCursor.lastReadMessage.createdAt` (fallback `lastReadAt`), overridable by `sinceIso`.

Both register natively via `toolTriggerSettings` (no `registerAiTools`, no table), only ever call `client.query` (read-only, C6), and fail closed: private channel + absent membership → typed `CHANNEL_FORBIDDEN` (explicit `canReadChannel` re-assert as defense in depth), missing/unauthorized → `CHANNEL_NOT_FOUND`, blank input → `INVALID_INPUT`.

## Checks (Tier 0 app-package gates)
- `yarn test:unit` → **54 pass / 0 fail** (was 29; +25 new)
- `yarn typecheck` and `npx tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` → exit 0
- `yarn lint` → 0 warnings / 0 errors
- `npx twenty dev:build .` → Build succeeded; manifest lists both tools with `toolTriggerSettings.required = ["channelId"]`

Notable decision: pinned `twenty-sdk@2.31.0` doesn't export `LogicFunctionExecutionContext`, so the tools declare the single field they consume rather than bumping the dependency (documented in the report). `PLAN.md` untouched, nothing committed; phase report + `.ralph-tui/progress.md` entries appended. Report goes to `phase-05-report.md`.

